      "message": "perf(ui): triangulate the area preview once per draft, not on each frame\n\nThe Boundary group's preview now keeps the triangles of its fill. The\npreview refresh makes them with the region, under the same key (draft\nparameters, draft area, source, document version). The scene reads the\nstored triangles. Release, fig8 state c of the #2238 probe: scene\n18.20 -> 2.76 ms, still frame 30.0 -> 14.8 ms. Display only.\n\nPinned by frame_cost_probe::still_frames_on_fig8_name_their_costs (no\ntriangulation on a still frame) and\nframe_cost_probe::area_preview_fill_is_made_once_per_draft (draft edit,\napply and undo rebuild the fill; still frames keep it).\n\nFixes #2246\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
